> <start_of_turn>user
In three sentences, explain what unified memory on the AMD Ryzen AI MAX+ 395 (Strix Halo) APU lets you do when running a 27-billion-parameter LLM in BF16 that a 32 GB discrete GPU cannot.<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
Unified memory on the Ryzen AI MAX+ 395 APU pools the system RAM and APU memory into a single, large resource, allowing it to load and run a 27B parameter LLM in BF16 *entirely* within that combined pool—something a 32GB discrete GPU cannot do due to its limited VRAM. This eliminates the need to offload layers to slower system RAM, resulting in significantly faster inference speeds and lower latency for large language models. Essentially, it unlocks the ability to run models that simply wouldn't fit on a typical dedicated GPU without performance-crippling workarounds.
